  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is which modality (RNA, image, or both) provides the strongest signal for this task. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible RNA baseline: it uses the most standard and computationally straightforward RNA encoder (PCA to 2000 dims) with a single profile, requiring no aggregation or fusion. Establishing this clean RNA baseline first allows me to (1) anchor all subsequent comparisons, (2) directly compare against an image-only baseline (config_010) and a multimodal baseline (config_016) in the next two experiments to answer the modality question, and (3) identify whether RNA alone is already competitive, which would shift the search toward encoder/aggregation refinements rather than fusion strategies. Starting with the simplest configuration avoids confounding multiple design choices and maximizes the interpretability of the first data point under a tight 10-experiment budget."
}

